---
export const title = 'Usage';
export const order = 100;
import DemoComponentCard from '../../../../components/DemoComponentCard.astro';
---

<p>
  <code>wc-relative-time</code> shows <code>datetime</code> (ISO 8601) relative to now, such as
  "5 minutes ago" or "in 3 days", in the page's locale. Hover it for the absolute date and time.
  It keeps itself current: every relative time on the page shares one timer, which refreshes each
  one as often as its text can change and pauses while the page is hidden.
</p>

<DemoComponentCard lang={'html'}>
  <div id='relative-time-demo' style='display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.5rem;'>
    <span>Edited <wc-relative-time data-ago='20000'></wc-relative-time></span>
    <span>Commented <wc-relative-time data-ago='300000'></wc-relative-time></span>
    <span>Created <wc-relative-time data-ago='86400000'></wc-relative-time></span>
    <span>Due <wc-relative-time data-ago='-259200000'></wc-relative-time></span>
  </div>
  <script is:inline>
    document.querySelectorAll('#relative-time-demo wc-relative-time').forEach(function (el) {
      el.datetime = new Date(Date.now() - Number(el.dataset.ago)).toISOString();
    });
  </script>
</DemoComponentCard>

<p>
  Content inside the element is shown while <code>datetime</code> is missing or not a date, and
  before the component loads, so put the absolute date there for pages rendered on the server.
</p>
